# Pre-commit gate. Runs `lint-staged`, which itself runs `eslint --fix`
# (Next.js core-web-vitals config) on every staged .js / .jsx file
# and re-stages any auto-fixes. ESLint errors fail the commit;
# warnings pass through.
#
# Why not `npm run build`? The full Next build takes 30-60 s on this
# codebase — too slow to run on every commit. Vercel runs the build
# on every push, so a broken build still gets caught before deploy,
# just one step later. If a class of regression starts slipping
# through to Vercel and getting noticed there too late, escalate to
# `next lint` (project-wide, ~5 s) here in the hook.

npx lint-staged
